 ### [Curvature-Controlled Style Contours](5350-curvature-controlled-style-contours.md)
-Curvature-Controlled Style Contours is a non-photorealistic volume rendering technique that generates outline contours with consistent visual thickness by regulating the detection threshold based on the normal curvature along the view direction. Unlike standard dot-product contours, which produce uncontrolled thickness variations (too thick on flat surfaces, too thin on fine structures), this method ensures that contours remain perceptually uniform across varying surface geometries. It builds on [Outline and Contour Generation](4137-outline-and-contour-generation.md) by integrating curvature-aware edge detection with style transfer functions for color mapping.
+Generates outline contours with consistent visual thickness by regulating the detection threshold based on the normal curvature along the view direction. Unlike standard dot-product contours, which produce uncontrolled thickness variations (too thick on flat surfaces, too thin on fine structures), this method ensures that contours remain perceptually uniform across varying surface geometries. It builds on [Outline and Contour Generation](4137-outline-and-contour-generation.md) by integrating curvature-aware edge detection with style transfer functions for color mapping [G].
 
 ### [Silhouette Rendering](7959-silhouette-rendering.md)
-Silhouette rendering is an object-space line rendering technique that extracts and stylizes significant edges (silhouettes and feature lines) from volumetric or surface data to enhance perceptual clarity and context. It distinguishes itself from image-space methods by processing geometry directly, allowing for precise hidden line removal and independent stroke stylization before compositing. It is particularly used to discriminate object classes based on specific features, such as highlighting lymph nodes touching critical structures in surgical planning.
+An object-space line rendering technique that extracts and stylizes significant edges (silhouettes and feature lines) from volumetric or surface data to enhance perceptual clarity and context. It distinguishes itself from image-space methods by processing geometry directly, allowing for precise hidden line removal and independent stroke stylization before compositing. It is particularly used to discriminate object classes based on specific features, such as highlighting lymph nodes touching critical structures in surgical planning.
 
 ### [Topological Landscape](8481-topological-landscape.md)
-Topological landscape is a visualization method that maps the topological structure of a scalar field's contour tree onto a 3D terrain model to enhance the perceptual clarity of volumetric features. It solves the problem of interpreting complex topological changes (merges and splits) in high-dimensional data by leveraging human intuition for reading terrain structures. It sets itself apart from direct volume rendering by abstracting the scalar field into a structural graph representation, and from other contour-based methods like [Outline and Contour Generation](4137-outline-and-contour-generation.md) by explicitly encoding topological events as geometric elevations rather than screen-space edges.
+A visualization method that maps a scalar field's contour tree onto a 3D terrain model to enhance the perceptual clarity of volumetric features. It solves the problem of interpreting complex topological changes in high-dimensional data by leveraging human intuition for reading terrain structures. It sets itself apart from direct volume rendering by presenting topological events as a navigable 3D terrain rather than a direct scalar projection.
 
 ### [Boundary Enhancement Volume Style](10863-boundary-enhancement-volume-style.md)
-Boundary Enhancement Volume Style is a non-photorealistic rendering technique designed to highlight feature bounds within volumetric data while simultaneously reducing visual noise. It addresses the challenge of distinguishing meaningful structures in continuous volumetric fields where feature areas are not well-defined as they are in surface-based rendering. Unlike sibling methods that focus on silhouette or contour lines, this style operates directly on volume boundaries to enhance perceptual clarity through edge emphasis.
+A non-photorealistic rendering technique that highlights feature bounds and reduces visual noise in volumetric data. It operates within a composite rendering graph to enhance perceptual clarity of continuous volumetric fields where feature areas are not well-defined as in surface-based rendering[G].
 
 ### [Suggestive Contour Extraction](13101-suggestive-contour-extraction.md)
-Suggestive contour extraction identifies surface locations where radial curvature is zero but increasing towards the viewer, complementing standard geometric contours to enhance shape perception. Unlike standard contours which mark the silhouette of the object relative to the camera, suggestive contours reveal the "hidden" curvature of the surface, particularly on convex regions, providing a more complete line drawing of the volume's form.
+Identifies surface locations where radial curvature is zero but increasing towards the viewer, complementing standard geometric contours to enhance shape perception. Unlike standard contours which mark the silhouette of the object relative to the camera, suggestive contours reveal the "hidden" curvature of the surface, particularly on convex regions, providing a more complete line drawing of the volume's form.
 
 #### Ghosted Views with Contours
-Ghosted Views with Contours is a technique where occluding context objects are reduced to contours to reveal pre-segmented internal structures [S1, unofficial]. The process involves:
-1.  Pre-segmenting the most interesting internal structures (e.g., small internal organs) [S1, unofficial].
-2.  Identifying context information (e.g., the body) that obscures the interesting structures [S1, unofficial].
-3.  In areas of occlusion, reducing the visual representation of the context object to contours [S1, unofficial].
+A variant where context objects are reduced to contours to reveal pre-segmented internal structures [S1, unofficial].
